8rt|v|To strike or thump, so as to rebound, or to make a sudden noise; a knock loudly. ; To leap or spring suddenly or unceremoniously; to bound; as, she bounced into the room. ; To boast; to talk big; to bluster. ; To drive against anything suddenly and violently; to bump; to thump. ; To cause to bound or rebound; sometimes, to toss. ; To eject violently, as from a room; to discharge unceremoniously, as from employment. ; To bully; to scold.	o:zfo,62,7~zfo,62,7	D:5y1,48,5;4m6,29,1~5y1,48,5;4m6,29,1
